{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And he said, The people cannot ascend.</b> The Gaon [Saadia] said that he pondered this verse for many years and did not know its meaning, until he saw in a book of the customs of the kings of Persia that an emissary has no permission to say to the king, 'I have fulfilled your mission,' until the king commands him to do another thing — then he may say it to him. In my opinion, because HaShem said to him, 'lest they break through to YHWH to see,' Moses did not know whether he needed to warn them not to look, for he had already warned them about the boundary not to cross it. Then HaShem said to him, Go descend, as I have commanded you, that you may testify against them, for Israel needed him to testify against them a second time."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:36:02.256035492Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}